   "evidence": "`CoordinateRealification.lean:312` changes to `simp [-splitCoords_symm_apply]`, with a comment saying the new simp lemma blocks `Fin.append_right` (`Mathlib/Data/Fin/Tuple/Basic.lean:330`, stated for `natAdd m i`) when the block sizes are equal.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Topology/Algebra/Module/Equiv/Fin.lean",
   "fix": "Add a high-priority `@[simp]` lemma `splitCoords_append : splitCoords n m (Fin.append a b) = (a, b)`, or a variant covering the `addNat` form, so the simp set closes the round-trip. Then go back to plain `simp` in `realifyCoords_complexifyCoords`. Otherwise, drop `@[simp]` from `splitCoords_symm_apply`.",
   "issue": "The `@[simp]` on `splitCoords_symm_apply` misfires: simp rewrites the inner `.symm` to `Fin.append` before `apply_symm_apply` can fire. With equal block sizes, the result `Fin.append a b (Fin.natAdd n i)` becomes an `addNat` form that `Fin.append_right` does not match, so the round-trip `splitCoords (splitCoords.symm x)` no longer simplifies.",
   "line": 46
  }
 ],
